## B. Candidate Priorities & Criterion-by-Criterion Scoring

The following 15 candidate healthcare improvement priorities have been defined and evaluated against six standard criteria. Each criterion is scored on a **1 to 5 scale**:
* **C1: Winter Magnitude** (1 = Minimal impact on winter pressure; 5 = Major direct reduction in winter ED/acute admissions)
* **C2: Strength of Evidence** (1 = Anecdotal/weak; 5 = Robust systematic review/RCT level evidence)
* **C3: Cost-Effectiveness / ROI** (1 = High cost/poor return; 5 = Highly cost-effective / rapid cash or capacity release)
* **C4: Strategic Alignment** (1 = Poor fit; 5 = Perfect alignment with NHS Long Term Plan & UK Life Sciences Vision)
* **C5: Timeframe to Impact** (1 = >10 years; 3 = 3–5 years; 5 = Direct impact within 1–3 years)
* **C6: Health Inequalities Impact** (1 = May worsen gap; 5 = Significant potential to reduce health disparities)

```
Criteria Weightings (Total = 100%):
• C1: Magnitude of Winter Problem (20%)
• C2: Strength of Evidence Base (20%)
• C3: Cost-Effectiveness & ROI (20%)
• C4: Alignment with NHS Plan & Life Sciences Strategy (15%)
• C5: Timeframe to Impact (15%)
• C6: Impact on Health Inequalities (10%)
```

